course: dictionary
lesson: 9127
title: Smug: too pleased with yourself
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Smug means too pleased with yourself, especially about your own cleverness, luck or goodness, in a way that annoys other people. The clues in «Big brothers are sometimes smug» show it: the word sometimes tells you the person is not always like this.
explain: Smug can also describe a look or smile that shows this feeling. Chinese has a word for it too: wǒ yíng le means I won, and if you shout it too loudly, people call you déyì, which means smug.
explain: In stories, a smug character usually shows off or looks down on others, so the reader often does not like them. Ask yourself how the other people in the sentence feel. If they feel annoyed, smug is probably the right word.
fact: Smug means too pleased with yourself, in a way that annoys other people.
fact: «A smug smile» is a smile that shows you think you are better than others.
fact: «Smugly» means in a smug way.
fact: «Don't be so smug!» is what you might say to a winner who boasts.
fact: Smug is an adjective, and its comparison forms are smugger and smuggest.
exercise: «Big brothers are sometimes smug.» What does smug mean? | *Too pleased with yourself, in a way that annoys others | Very kind and gentle | Scared of the dark | Sleepy after a long day
exercise: Ella wins the spelling test, grins at everyone and says, «I knew I'd win!» Which word best describes her? | sleepy | *smug | sorry | shy
exercise: Which word in the lessons means smug in Chinese? | dreich | wǒ yíng le, meaning I won | *déyì
test: What does a smug smile show? | That the person is lost | *That the person is too pleased with themselves | That the person is cold | That the person is hungry
test: Which sentence shows a smug person best? | The little sister said sorry and shared her sweets. | *The winner kept saying how clever she was and looked down on the others. | The boy cried quietly in the corner. | The dog slept by the fire.
exam: What is the best meaning of smug? | Quiet and gentle, like a whisper | *Too pleased with yourself, in a way that annoys other people | Very old and worn out | Hungry after a long walk
